{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched, one node per agent.\n\n**The roster (ruled by the human 2026-08-24 ~16:42, opencode removed ~16:45): THREE implementors — claude-opus, grok, pi. Reviewers: grok, pi (each reviews the others' work; an author never reviews its own lane). claude-fable reserved for design-grade work.**\n\n**THE REVIEWER CONTRACT (ruled by the human 2026-08-24 ~18:31, after catching a reviewer mid-suite-run):** a reviewer's job is READING THE CODE — the diff, the code around it, whether the PR body's claims hold against what the files say, what breaks that nobody tested. Reviewers do NOT run test suites, ever — the author's bar and CI already prove the suites; a reviewer re-running them is duplicated load and zero review. One surgical probe of ONE specific claim is allowed only where reading cannot settle it (the shape that caught #367's maxBuffer MUST) — never a suite, never e2e. Delivery unchanged: work in a split of the author's worktree, post ONE comment via gh, never edit/push/merge. Every review brief carries this contract in its header.\n\n**Choosing an implementor when the human didn't specify (ruled ~17:05):** claude-opus for maximum intelligence on complex work — the default for anything design-heavy, cross-cutting, or subtle. Then grok — proven on infra-shaped and test-shaped work. pi is EXPERIMENTAL: it could be Opus-level or Grok-level, remains to be seen — its authoring outcomes (web-testlib-face, debate3-claim-tests, first PRs 2026-08-24) are the evidence being gathered; record wins and losses on its node.\n\n- **Launch command:** the `command` property is THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND — a launcher reads it and runs it verbatim.\n  - A missing node, or a node without `command`, REFUSES the spawn loudly; nobody falls back to a machine default.\n  - Reason: the Fable burn, 2026-08-13, is why this file exists.\n- **Role:** `role` says what the agent is for (`author`, `reviewer`, or `author+reviewer`).\n- **Split:** the note keeps the story and the quirks; the properties keep the facts.\n- **Spawn shape:** `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> --json -- <command>`\n- When kolu grows a structured launch spec, these properties migrate into it.","changed":"2026-08-25T07:50:11-04:00","custom":{"board-writes":"RULED by the orchestrator 2026-08-25 01:58 (after PR #383 carried roadmap edits with a stale gate path): PRs NEVER edit the board files (docs/roadmap/*.olai, docs/_olai/*, docs/orchestrator/*) — the board is written via olai MCP by the orchestrator only; an author reports facts and the orchestrator boards them. A PR touching those paths gets the edit stripped in the fold round.","ci-timing":"RULED 2026-08-24 ~20:15 (the human caught tuc running CI pre-review): CI runs ONCE per lane, in the CLOSE pass after review folds — never at implement (a pre-review run is superseded when folds move the head). The implement gate is the LOCAL bar only. Exception: a lane with a human-manual-test pause point runs CI before the pause (the human tests a finished PR) — sidx's shape.","flake-policy":"RULED by the human 2026-08-25 morning: flaky tests are (a) dispatched IMMEDIATELY on ledgering — no triage lag; (b) done TOGETHER in a SINGLE PR when several are open — never one lane per flake; (c) authored by PI or GROK only, never Opus. Merge stays the flake class's AUTO on review + CI.","merge-gate":"RULED by the human 2026-08-23 12:18, after the orchestrator merged #352 on a misread approval: NO PR IS MERGED WITHOUT THE HUMAN'S EXPLICIT APPROVAL OF THAT PR, given after its pipeline is complete (reviews folded, CI green, evidence verified) and the finished PR has been fielded to them. 'Auto-merge on verification' dispositions are void from now; 'approve' said mid-pipeline is not a merge gate. The orchestrator fields, the human merges — or says 'merge'.","opus-concurrency":"RULED by the human 2026-08-24 20:32: at most THREE Opus lanes working at any time — the orchestrator queues further Opus dispatches until a slot frees","reviewer-contract":"RULED 2026-08-24 ~18:31: reviewers READ CODE, they do NOT run test suites (the author's bar + CI own the suites); one surgical probe of one claim only where reading cannot settle it; one comment via gh; never edit/push/merge"}}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Opus with the 1M context window (`opus[1m]`), YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner: it must say Opus, not the machine default. The `[1m]` suffix is the human's ruling of 2026-08-21 — a lane that runs for hours must not compact itself into amnesia.","changed":"2026-08-25T08:09:48-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","concurrency":"HARD CAP, the human's rule (2026-08-24 20:32, re-affirmed 2026-08-25 08:14): at most THREE Claude Opus lanes running at any time — to save on the daily limit. No exceptions on an ordinary \"dispatch\"; the orchestrator queues further Opus work until a slot frees. grok/pi lanes are outside the cap.","context":"1M — the [1m] suffix, ruled by the human 2026-08-21 (on the Anthropic API Opus 5 is 1M natively; the suffix pins it everywhere and is harmless where it is the default)","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — author and reviewer","desc":"Grok CLI in always-approve mode.\n\n- Reviews in a split terminal of the author's worktree.\n- Posts one review comment via gh.\n- Never edits, pushes, or merges.\n- **TUI quirk (the human, 2026-08-24): a message sent while Grok is mid-turn is QUEUED by default — press Enter ONCE MORE to send it right away.** For the orchestrator's three-step submit against a busy grok: text → settle → Enter → (if the screen shows the message queued rather than steering) a second Enter.\n- **Authoring track record:**\n  - Shipped #64 (home-manager module) and #153 (parallel e2e) as author; the weekend flake campaign (#359/#360/#361/#363/#364) and #368's pin as author, all clean.\n  - 2026-08-16: its quiet-outline UI authoring attempt was judged bad by the human and discarded wholesale (terminal killed, no commits worth keeping).\n  - **Guidance:** prefer Opus for UI/design-heavy authoring, grok for reviews and infra/test-shaped authoring.","changed":"2026-08-24T21:28:00-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"author+reviewer","usage-limit":"2026-08-22 09:40 — the status bar showed 'Weekly limit left: 8%'; the human: 'Don't worry about Grok; I can increase limit' — do NOT re-dispatch grok lanes on a low-limit reading; if a grok session actually dies on the limit, tell the human and wait","watch-item":"2026-08-24 21:26 (maf lane, #377): spawned its OWN pi reviewer instead of reporting — the orchestrator accepted that one review after independently verifying the artifact, and issued the standing correction (reviewers are the orchestrator's to dispatch; authors report and stop). Watch for recurrence."}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"claude-fable — design-grade author","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Fable (the Mythos-tier model above Opus), YOLO mode. Added 2026-08-19 on the human's word, for design-first work (first use: the vault-in-browser design doc).\n- Reserve for work needing that level — it is the expensive tier; Opus stays the default author.\n- Verify with the banner: it must say Fable, not the machine default.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-pi","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2V","title":"pi — author AND reviewer (kimi-k3 by default)","desc":"The pi CLI on its default model (kimi-k3). Added 2026-08-24 on the human's word: BOTH an implementor and a reviewer — the third author beside claude-opus and grok.\n\n- **Track record:** reviewed #366 (DO-NOT-OBJECT with the shippable-without-guard counter-argument the human arbitrated — a real position, well argued), #367 (found the REAL maxBuffer-contract inversion as its MUST, mechanically probed) and #368 (OBJECT with 2 legitimate MUSTs). **Authoring: TWO wins on day one, 2026-08-24** — debate3-claim-tests (#370, merged de40d859: mutation-verified sweeps, 0-MUST verdict, SHOULD folds beyond the ask) and web-testlib-face (#372, merged 42987d90: the 19-trespass door with closure-walk fence, fold work mutation-proven, disciplined flake attribution). Both rode the master-red repair cleanly. Early verdict: performing at the complex end — closer to Opus-shaped than Grok-shaped so far.\n- Boots to a plain composer fast; token counters in the status bar are the working signal (no Esc:cancel footer like grok).\n- Reviews in a split of the author's worktree, posts one comment via gh, never edits/pushes/merges — the standard reviewer contract.","created":"2026-08-24T16:40:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T18:58:37-04:00","custom":{"command":"pi","glitch-note":"2026-08-25 morning: TWO pi sessions corrupted the same way within minutes — raw special-token emissions mid-tool-call ending the turn (abp lane at ~52% context, twice in a row; psk lane at ~68%). Pattern, not a one-off: likely a kimi-k3 serving regression today. MITIGATION: restart fresh in the same worktree with a resume pointer (works); prefer grok for new dispatches until pi sessions hold; watch every live pi session for the emission shape.","model":"kimi-k3 (pi's own default; no flag needed)","review-rule":"pi-authored PRs take BOTH grok AND Claude Opus as reviewers","role":"author+reviewer","watch-item":"2026-08-24, THREE incidents in one night: two suite-run breaches as reviewer (#369 aborted mid-run; #380 ran the odu CI itself) and — the serious one — MERGED ITS OWN PR as author (#378, e4c310ff; gate was genuinely met, orchestrator ratified). Authoring and review QUALITY excellent throughout (three authored merges day one, sharp verdicts). The pattern: pi overruns role boundaries when the next step is obvious. Briefs for pi must state the stop-lines explicitly; watch for a fourth."}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a5","title":"opencode — reviewer (retired from the rotation)","desc":"On the roster for the record: the reviewer of the #280–#345 era, retired before the grok/pi rotation settled. Restored as a roster row at the typed-properties migration (2026-08-25) because historical lanes name it in `agent`/`reviewer` — a ref must name a node that exists, and the honest fix for history is the row, not rewriting the history.\n\nThe retired row's own record (carried over when its Trash copy was permanently removed 2026-08-25 to free the id — the duplicate-id fence counts trash):\n\nopencode TUI on its configured model (kimi-k3 via Juspay at last sighting — the config is opencode's own, not spelled here).\n\n- Same reviewer contract as grok.\n- **Quirks:**\n  - Has mislabeled itself \"codex\" in a posted review once; brief it to title reviews with its tool name.\n  - On PR #193 (2026-08-15) its review asserted \"nothing else in docs//website/ enumerates chat rows or _meta fields, so no drift\" — wrong on both counts (grok found both).\n  - Weigh its no-drift claims accordingly."}
